I'd just like to take this moment to point out that the owners of RPG Maker have never been shy about deleting important work and data, as evidenced by how the only way today to view the officially-sanctioned Indie Game Maker Contest 2014 (formerly located at
http://contest.rpgmakerweb.com/
) and IGMC 2015 (formerly located at
http://contest.gamedevfort.com/
) is via the Wayback Machine. Frankly speaking, I'm certain that the only reason future contests were preserved is because they were hosted via itch.io.
You'd think that archiving official contests would be important for demonstrating what's possible in your engines, along with showing the passion and talent of your userbase, but alas.

